        "original_id": "007e8e32-9de7-5691-a22e-1e5329ed20e6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Nostalgia (2018 film)\n- People: Mark Pellington, Alex Ross Perry, Patton Oswalt, Jon Hamm, Nick Offerman, Amber Tamblyn, Catherine Keener, Ellen Burstyn, Bruce Dern, John Ortiz, James LeGros\n- Topics: American drama films, stand-up comedy, acting, voice acting, writing\n\nFacts:\n- Nostalgia is an upcoming American drama film directed by Mark Pellington and written by Mark Pellington and Alex Ross Perry.\n- Nostalgia stars Jon Hamm, Nick Offerman, Amber Tamblyn, Patton Oswalt, Catherine Keener, Ellen Burstyn, Bruce Dern, John Ortiz, and James LeGros.\n- Patton Peter Oswalt was born on January 27, 1969, and he is an American stand-up comedian, actor, voice actor, and writer.\n- From 1998 to 2007, Patton Oswalt played Spencer Olchin in the sitcom The King of Queens.\n- In 2007, Patton Oswalt voiced Remy in the film Ratatouille.\n- From 2014 to 2017, Patton Oswalt played multiple identical brothers called the Koenigs on Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D.\n- Patton Oswalt played male Jesse in both seasons of Minecraft Story Mode.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
